  <title>Make your first lab</title>
  <p>A lab is a project: its bricks, the events that start and stop them, and the disk images of its machines. The smallest useful one is a switch and a virtual machine plugged into it. You need a disk image for the machine, as a <file>.qcow2</file> file with a system installed.</p>
  <steps>
    <item>
      <p>In the <gui>Bricks</gui> tab, click <gui>New Brick</gui> and choose <gui>Switch</gui>. The switch is named <sys>sw1</sys>, and its settings show: click <gui>OK</gui>.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <p>Click <gui>New Brick</gui> again and choose <gui>Virtual machine</gui>. It is named <sys>vm1</sys>, and its settings show.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <p>Under <gui>Disks</gui>, click <gui>Add Disk</gui>. In the list of images of the new disk, choose <gui>Add an Existing Image…</gui>, then the file of your disk image.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <p>Under <gui>Network</gui>, click <gui>Add Card</gui>, and choose <sys>sw1</sys> in <gui>Plugged into</gui>.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <p>Click <gui>OK</gui>.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <p>Click the start button of <sys>vm1</sys>, in its row. The switch starts first, since the machine plugs into it, and both rows say <gui>Running</gui>.</p>
    </item>
  </steps>
  <figure>
    <title>The first lab, running</title>
    <media type="image" mime="image/png" src="figures/first-lab.png">
      <p>The Bricks tab with two rows, both Running: sw1, a switch of 32 ports, and vm1, a virtual machine of 64 MiB whose card eth0 is on sw1.</p>
    </media>
  </figure>
  <p>The disk is a <gui>Private copy</gui> of the image: the machine writes its changes to a file of its own, in the folder of the project, and the image stays as it is. See <link xref="images"/>.</p>
  <p>Virtualbricks saves the project every three minutes and when it quits. To save it now, choose <guiseq><gui>Projects</gui><gui>Save</gui></guiseq>, or press <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>S</key></keyseq>.</p>
  <note style="tip">
    <p>The same lab from the console of Virtualbricks:</p>
    <screen>image add debian ~/images/debian.qcow2
brick new switch
brick new vm
brick set vm1 hda_image=debian
brick card add vm1 plug sw1
brick start vm1</screen>
    <p>See <link xref="console"/>.</p>
  </note>
</page>
